---

<BrandGuide
  brandKey="adidas"
  brand="Adidas"
  title="Adidas Size Chart & Fit Guide: Does It Run Big?"
  description="Adidas shoes tend to run about half a size big, especially Originals, so many size down. Apparel is roomy in Originals, slimmer in performance lines."
  fitSections={fitSections}
  faqs={faqs}
  related={related}
>
  <Fragment slot="verdict">
    <strong>Adidas footwear tends to run big</strong> — Originals like the Superstar, Stan Smith,
    and Samba are commonly reported to fit about half a size large, so many shoppers size down.
    Apparel splits by line: Originals clothing leans roomy and boxy, while performance pieces are
    cut slimmer and closer to the chart. Know which line you're buying before you pick a size.
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="tips">
    <li><strong>Sort by silhouette, not brand:</strong> half a size down is common in Originals sneakers, while Ultraboost and running models tend to fit true.</li>
    <li><strong>Coming from Nike?</strong> The brands lean opposite ways, so your Nike size is a starting point at best: re-measure rather than transfer the number.</li>
    <li><strong>Check the line on apparel:</strong> Originals cuts run relaxed for the retro look; training and Techfit pieces are meant to sit close to the body.</li>
    <li><strong>Wide feet change the math:</strong> shoppers with wider feet often skip the size-down advice in Originals to keep toe-box room.</li>
  </Fragment>
</BrandGuide>
